// The count of Socket.read_bytes() must be an integer, and an integer is an
// Int or an integer-valued Number (spec/05-stdlib.md, Integer arguments). The
// Int count reads the same two bytes; a fractional count is a runtime error
// that halts the program.
// COVERS: integer-arg socket-read-bytes
// STATUS: error
// TIMEOUT: 10
// CHECK: ab
var l = listen("127.0.0.1", 0);
var c = connect("127.0.0.1", l.port());
var s = l.accept();
c.write("abcdef");
print s.read_bytes(2i);
s.read_bytes(2.5);
print "unreachable";
